# Build and dependency output. LEADING SLASHES ARE LOAD-BEARING: an unanchored
# `name/` pattern matches that directory name at ANY depth, so `coverage/`
# silently swallowed the whole of `src/coverage/` — this package's coverage
# NORMALIZERS, real source, never committed and never noticed, because git does
# not warn about a file it was told to ignore. `src/analysis/walk.ts` documents
# the identical bug in the source walk and fixes it the same way: build-output
# names are output only at the REPO ROOT. Anchor every one of them.
/node_modules/
/dist/
# kragg local artifacts (journal, coverage, criticality, mutation sessions).
# NOTE the `/*` — git cannot re-include a file inside an excluded DIRECTORY,
# so `.kragg/` would make the negation below a silent no-op.
.kragg/*
# Accepted equivalent mutants are a reviewed, shared property of the codebase,
# so this one artifact is deliberately tracked. See src/commands/mutation/baseline.ts.
!.kragg/mutants.baseline
/coverage/
*.tsbuildinfo
.DS_Store
.env
.env.*
